		summary = "**Nashville** is the capital and most populous city in the U.S. state of [[Tennessee]]. It is the [[County seat|seat]] of Davidson County in Middle Tennessee, located on the Cumberland River. It is the 20th-most populous city in the United States and fourth-most populous city in [[Southeastern United States|the Southeast]], with a population of 689,447 at the 2020 census (estimated at 721,074 in 2025). The Nashville metropolitan area, with over 2.15 million people, is the [[Metropolitan statistical area|35th-largest metropolitan area]] in the country. Nashville is among the fastest-growing cities in the U.S.",
